 BrownBear can install and run **browser extensions** (Chrome/Edge/Firefox `.crx`/`.zip`/`.xpi`), the
 way [Orion](https://kagi.com/orion/) and [Gear Browser](https://gear4.app/) do — not just userscripts.
+Before an archive from a store page, pasted link, curated recommendation, or local file is written
+to disk, every path asks the user to review its required API permissions, host access, content-script
+matches, and optional permissions that may be requested later. Cancelling a reinstall leaves the
+installed copy in place. The review is based on the package manifest; it does not scan the extension's
+code or certify safety. Optional access still requires a separate prompt when requested at runtime.
